    board(ops): file CF-206 — the fleet ops census classifies code-factory as `docs`
    
    The ops lane's first tick (code-factory-ops-2026-11-04-23-33-53) ran the census
    (`fleet_ops_check.py --project code-factory`, rc=0, "flagged 0 of 1 families")
    and read the kind column instead of the verdict: code-factory is judged on
    nothing, because `docs_only` is derived from the absence of a language manifest
    and `ops_gaps()` emits zero checks for kind=docs.
    
    Consequence: 8 executable operational scripts (node-create.sh, project-node.sh,
    verify-node.sh, bunker-server-install.sh, boardctl, lane_target.py,
    disk_floor.py, clone_lane.py) and the node-provisioning/supervision surface
    never reach an ops question. Measured class scope: 5 of 45 docs-classified
    families carry shell tooling — code-factory (8), code-factory-duckbrain (8),
    fleet-ops-check (183), h3 (24), my-project (2).
    
    The row carries a one-line re-runnable probe (prints `docs` today) and six
    acceptance criteria, including a three-fixture no-regression leg and a
    committed-patch leg (the live script is unversioned and was edited 20 minutes
    before this tick).
    
    Guard: board-only diff refuses with the documented Tier-1 DEGRADED PASS, so
    this commit takes the disclosed `core.hooksPath=/dev/null` bypass.
    Gates at this tree: boardctl validate RESULT: OK (4 pre-existing warnings),
    tests/selftest.sh SELFTEST: PASS.
