+{"id":"CF-206","title":"P2 — the fleet ops census classifies code-factory as `docs` and judges it on nothing: 8 operational scripts and the node-provisioning surface sit outside every ops check","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 by the ops lane's first tick (code-factory-ops-2026-11-04-23-33-53) at tip 53d39f4 with tracked porcelain clean and origin/main...HEAD = 0 0.\n\nThe lane ran its own census: `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project code-factory` prints \"OPS CENSUS  1 project families  docs=1\", \"flagged 0 of 1 families\", rc=0. The rc is the clean verdict; the `kind` column is the finding.\n\nWhy it says docs: fleet_ops_check.py:285 derives `docs_only` as \"none of go.mod, package.json, pyproject.toml, setup.py, Cargo.toml, requirements.txt exists\", classify() at :172 then returns 'docs', and ops_gaps() at :181 runs its checks only for service/cli/library — so a `docs` family gets ZERO checks by design (\"a spec corpus has no uptime\").\n\ncode-factory has no language manifest but is not a spec corpus. It ships 8 executable operational scripts under scripts/ (node-create.sh, project-node.sh, verify-node.sh, bunker-server-install.sh, boardctl, lane_target.py, disk_floor.py, clone_lane.py), a harness/ adapter tree, and a tests/selftest.sh gate. It creates, verifies and supervises remote nodes; that is exactly the surface an ops census exists to interrogate.\n\nClass scope, measured the same tick from `--json` over the whole fleet plus `find <root>/scripts <root>/bin -maxdepth 2 -name '*.sh'`: 45 of 84 families classify as `docs` (cli=2, library=4, service=34, unknown=3), and 5 of those 45 carry shell tooling — code-factory (8 scripts), code-factory-duckbrain (8, same workdir), fleet-ops-check (183, workdir ~/.hermes), h3 (24, ~/get-h3/h3), my-project (2). So the hole also blinds h3 and the scanner's own family.\n\nMitigating measurement, so this is not filed as a false P1: docs/OPERATIONS.md exists, and DEPLOY_DOC includes 'docs/operations.md', so once this family classifies as `cli` it passes its deploy-doc check. The defect is INVISIBILITY — no ops question is ever asked of this family — not a specific missing artifact.\n\nCorroborating condition: ~/.hermes/scripts is not a git repository (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel` answers \"fatal: not a git repository\"), and fleet_ops_check.py was modified at 18:18 local on 2026-11-04 by another writer, 20 minutes before this tick. The census that every -ops lane depends on therefore has no version history and no rollback, which is why this row carries an acceptance criterion about capturing the change as a committed patch rather than accepting an in-place edit.\n\nReproduction today (repo root, one line):\npython3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project code-factory --json | jq -r '.[0].kind'\nprints `docs`.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree, from the repository root (this is the row's probe): `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project code-factory --json | jq -r '.[0].kind'` prints `docs` and exits 0 today.\n1. `classify()` in ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py detects a shell toolkit — at least two tracked `*.sh` files under `scripts/` or `bin/`, or a `tests/selftest.sh` gate — so `--project code-factory --json | jq -r '.[0].kind'` prints `cli` and the family is judged on deploy-doc.\n2. The `--json` evidence names the basis rather than only the verdict: `.[0].evidence.kind_basis` starts with `shell-toolkit:` and carries the script count (e.g. `shell-toolkit:8`).\n3. No regression in the existing kinds, proven with three fixtures: a manifest-less docs tree (only `docs/*.md`, no scripts) still prints `docs`; a tree with `go.mod` plus `cmd/` still prints `cli`; a tree with `package.json` and a Dockerfile still prints `service`.\n4. Census exit-code semantics unchanged, proven on two fixtures: rc=0 when no family has gaps, rc=1 when at least one does.\n5. Fleet delta recorded at the fixing tip: the `--json` census no longer reports 45 `docs` families; the closeout names the new counts and re-lists the five shell-toolkit families from this row's reasoning (code-factory, code-factory-duckbrain, fleet-ops-check, h3, my-project).\n6. The change is captured as a committed patch, because the live file is unversioned: `patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch` exists in the repository, `git apply --check patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch` succeeds at the fixing HEAD, and the row's closeout quotes its sha256.","probe":"python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project code-factory --json | jq -r '.[0].kind'","created_at":"2026-11-04T23:46:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T23:46:00Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"4b21e7096436cc23d6884b4ff54d9f61c976e0ec48000e1651d27e634532fd12"},"capability_tags":["ops","census","tooling"],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
